 "signs": [
  {
   "x": 9,
   "y": 20,
   "text": "STOREY ARMS. Start of the Pen y Fan path. It's mostly up. Mostly sideways in the rain."
  },
  {
   "x": 3,
   "y": 17,
   "text": "BANNAU BRYCHEINIOG (BRECON BEACONS). A National Park and an International Dark Sky Reserve. Stars, if the sky co-operates."
  },
  {
   "x": 44,
   "y": 16,
   "text": "PEN Y FAN, 886 m. The highest peak in southern Britain. You are at the top. Everyone else is also at the top. Mind the elbow."
  },
  {
   "x": 34,
   "y": 18,
   "text": "CORN DU, 873 m. Pen y Fan's less famous sibling. Good wind, no queue."
  },
  {
   "x": 23,
   "y": 23,
   "text": "SARN HELEN. A Roman road, still here after 1,900 years. Which is more than can be said for your umbrella."
  },
  {
   "x": 12,
   "y": 28,
   "text": "WILD PONIES. Do not feed. Do not pet. Do not ask them for directions."
  },
  {
   "x": 59,
   "y": 25,
   "text": "CARDIFF 20 miles. Downhill, mostly. The rain will come with you."
  },
  {
   "x": 2,
   "y": 15,
   "text": "ST DAVIDS 40 miles. Behind you. Good luck with that."
  },
  {
   "x": 40,
   "y": 20,
   "plaque": "beacons_old_red_sandstone",
   "title": "Old Red Sandstone",
   "text": "These hills are Old Red Sandstone, laid down by rivers around 400 million years ago in the Devonian period. It gives the paths their rusty colour, and a tough layer of it makes the flat tops of Pen y Fan and Corn Du. The ice ages did the sculpting."
  },
  {
   "x": 30,
   "y": 27,
   "plaque": "beacons_cwm_llwch",
   "title": "Llyn Cwm Llwch",
   "text": "Below Corn Du lies the little lake of Llyn Cwm Llwch. Legend says that every May Day a door opened in a rock by the water onto a fairy island, where visitors were feasted, until one guest pocketed a flower and the door shut for good. Moral: leave the flowers."
  },
  {
   "x": 25,
   "y": 36,
   "text": "ABERTAWE / SWANSEA 25 miles. Down the old drovers' lane to the sea, the market and the Mumbles. Gower beyond."
  },
  {
   "x": 4,
   "y": 15,
   "text": "DAN YR OGOF SHOW CAVES. Cathedral Cave, the Bone Cave and a river that rather fancies itself. Hard hats not provided. Sense of wonder, free."
  }
 ],
 "spawn": [
  2,
  19
 ],
